---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import ArticleSchema from '../../components/ArticleSchema.astro';
import FaqSection from '../../components/FaqSection.astro';
import { site, pageTitle } from '../../content';
const path = '/for/high-aov';
const title = pageTitle(site, 'for/high-aov');
const desc = 'Evaluate Shopify SMS for considered purchases: buyer authority, quote state, adviser handoffs, purchase exits and contribution after costs.';
const faqs = [
  {
    "question": "Does a high cart value justify more SMS follow-up?",
    "answer": "No. Use the requested next step, current permission and purchase state to decide whether a message is useful. A long consideration period is not permission for a fixed pursuit sequence."
  },
  {
    "question": "Can a gift recipient receive the buyer’s quote reminders?",
    "answer": "Keep buyer, recipient and adviser identities separate. A delivery phone number does not establish marketing permission or authority to approve a quote, financing or payment."
  },
  {
    "question": "When should a quote queue stop?",
    "answer": "Retire it on purchase, withdrawal, expired permission or quote, adviser takeover, or a conflicting support case. A retry or late event must not reopen a retired queue without a new validated request."
  },
  {
    "question": "How should high-AOV SMS performance be measured?",
    "answer": "Use mature paid orders and net sales after discounts and returns. Compare contribution per eligible customer with a holdout over the same consideration and return window; deposits and finance applications are separate milestones."
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="relative overflow-hidden py-16 md:py-24">
    <div class="container">
      <a href="/for" class="link text-sm">← All store types</a>
      <p class="badge mt-6">High-AOV stores</p>
      <h1 class="hero-title mt-5 max-w-5xl">Choosing Shopify SMS marketing apps for high-AOV stores</h1>
      <p class="mt-7 max-w-3xl text-xl leading-9 text-orange-950/80">An expensive purchase may need product evidence, a consultation, a quote or financing before checkout. Evaluate whether your workflow can send a requested next step to the right person while retiring every obsolete reminder.</p>
      <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-8 text-orange-950/75">A browse, deposit or finance application is not a completed purchase. A phone number on a delivery address is not evidence that its owner can authorize an order. Start with those distinctions before choosing software.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container pb-12">
    <div class="prose-shopify card">
      <h2>Conditional candidates, based on the job</h2>
      <p>Keep a working system if it passes your account tests. The following are candidates to evaluate, not a ranking or a required stack. Official capabilities were checked November 25, 2026; neither supplier page establishes that your quote, finance or adviser integration will work.</p>
      <ul>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://postscript.io/">Postscript</a> describes SMS list building and message sending. Consider it for a permissioned SMS next-step workflow if your installed account can consume current order and quote state, enforce exits and route replies to the responsible adviser. Verify each control in a sandbox or controlled pilot.</li>
        <li><a class="link" href="https://www.klaviyo.com/solutions/marketing-automation">Klaviyo</a> describes email, SMS and data integrations. Consider it where a team wants to coordinate education and SMS against shared customer state, provided the actual integrations preserve identity, event ordering and cross-channel suppression.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Ask suppliers to demonstrate appointment ownership, reply routing, destination coverage, consent evidence, exportable suppression and delayed-event handling on your account. Confirm plan access, implementation work, support escalation and current pricing in writing. Include messaging segments, carrier fees, contacts, integrations, adviser time and migration costs; no price or contract comparison is asserted here.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Separate identity, authority and permission</h2>
      <p>Maintain stable customer and opportunity identifiers plus separate roles for buyer, gift recipient, household adviser and assigned sales representative. Confirm who owns the phone number, who may approve a quote, who may apply for finance, who may pay a deposit and who may place or change the order. Do not merge people solely because an address or shared phone matches.</p>
      <p>A sales representative can explain product options and arrange an appointment within their assigned role; that does not give them authority to approve finance, reserve inventory or commit the buyer to payment. Use the authoritative quote, lender, reservation, order and payment systems for those decisions. Do not expose finance status or buyer details to a recipient or adviser without appropriate authorization.</p>
      <p>For each send, check the current purpose and channel permission, capture source, timestamp, disclosure and subsequent withdrawal. A consultation request, delivery contact or service update must not silently become permission for a promotional sequence. Keep email and SMS permissions distinct, honor applicable suppression and verify the rules and quiet hours for the destination with your compliance owner. If identity, timezone or permission is uncertain, hold the message for review.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Let the considered purchase set the next step</h2>
      <p>Use requested product education, fit checks, warranty information or a booked consultation to guide the journey. Send detailed comparisons through an appropriate requested channel; a short SMS can point to a requested appointment or current quote when permission supports it. Do not turn a long decision into a universal daily or weekly pursuit cadence.</p>
      <p>Assign one owner when the customer asks a question or books a representative. Record the appointment ID, owner, timezone, requested channel and acknowledgement. Pause automation during the handoff; if no representative accepts, create a visible support task instead of continuing sales reminders. A reschedule or cancellation replaces the old appointment version and retires its pending messages.</p>
      <p>Inventory availability, reservation expiry, quote version, price and financing terms must come from their current source at dispatch. A quote is not an inventory reservation; a deposit is not a paid balance; a finance application is not approval. Do not manufacture scarcity, promise a locked price after expiry or automatically add a discount to overcome hesitation. A changed price or unavailable item needs a fresh review and customer decision.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Queue retirement, retries and late events</h2>
      <p>Use an opportunity ID, state version and message-purpose key to deduplicate sends across representative tools, email and SMS. Before dispatch, recheck permission, holdout membership, quote and reservation validity, payment and order state, appointment ownership and support conflicts. Enforce exits at dispatch rather than relying only on a scheduled audience snapshot.</p>
      <p>Purchase retires the related acquisition queue across channels; withdrawal retires the requested pursuit and applies the relevant permission suppression. Quote expiry, reservation release, cancellation, open disputes and representative takeover also invalidate related reminders. Keep a durable retirement record and suppression history. A new request needs a new validated scope, not reuse of a stale queue.</p>
      <p>Retries must retain the same idempotency key. If delivery is uncertain, reconcile provider status before retrying; use bounded retries and an exception queue with an owner. Compare source versions and effective timestamps so a late browse or abandoned-checkout event cannot override a newer paid order or withdrawal. Reconcile missing events with the source of truth and fail closed when state is stale.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Proposed workload tests before a pilot</h2>
      <p>These are hypothetical fixtures, not merchant case studies or observed results. Run them against the actual integrations, record expected and actual state, and keep the program paused until failures are resolved.</p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Gift purchase:</strong> a buyer requests a furniture quote but supplies the recipient’s delivery number. Expect no buyer quote promotion to that number; resolve identity and permission separately.</li>
        <li><strong>Adviser handoff:</strong> an audio buyer asks a technical question and books a demo. Expect an acknowledged representative task, paused pursuit and no duplicate booking text from another channel.</li>
        <li><strong>Finance decision:</strong> an application arrives before lender approval. Expect no approval claim or payment demand; route questions to the authorized finance process without disclosing status to a household adviser.</li>
        <li><strong>Deposit and balance:</strong> a deposit posts while a cart reminder is pending. Expect the acquisition reminder to retire, with any requested balance update using the correct order, payer and amount. Do not count the deposit and final balance as two orders.</li>
        <li><strong>Limited edition:</strong> a collector has an expired reservation when a delayed availability event arrives. Expect no scarcity text or reservation promise until current inventory, entitlement and price are verified.</li>
        <li><strong>Quote change:</strong> an approved quote version is superseded during a retry. Expect the stale link and amount to be blocked; a representative confirms the revised proposal through the permitted channel.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdrawal:</strong> a customer declines while an old browse event and a duplicate webhook arrive. Expect durable retirement and no reopened pursuit from replay or retry.</li>
        <li><strong>Purchase race:</strong> the order is paid just before dispatch and its event is delayed. Expect source reconciliation to suppress the reminder; alert an owner if the system cannot establish current state.</li>
        <li><strong>Support recovery:</strong> a delivery dispute opens before a promotional send. Expect a support handoff, paused sales messages and a named owner; closing the case alone must not silently restart the retired sequence.</li>
        <li><strong>Migration rollback:</strong> replay suppression, appointment and payment events in the replacement system, then stop it. Expect the old system to resume only verified eligible work, with identical retirement and dedupe history and no replayed backlog.</li>
      </ol>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Measure orders, customers and contribution separately</h2>
      <p>Define a paid-order denominator: unique completed orders in the measurement window, with deposits linked to the same order and cancellations and refunds reconciled. Define net sales consistently after discounts and returns, excluding tax and pass-through amounts according to your accounting policy. AOV is net sales divided by those orders; it is not revenue per message or per customer.</p>
      <p>For a customer-level experiment, assign eligible buyers to treatment or holdout before sending and keep their linked opportunities in the same arm. Report unique eligible customers per arm, purchasing customers divided by eligible customers, and mature paid orders divided by eligible customers. Count all assigned eligible customers, including those who received no message. Do not use delivered recipients as the holdout denominator.</p>
      <p>Contribution equals net sales less product cost, payment and finance fees borne by the store, fulfillment, shipping subsidy, return handling, support and representative labor, and allocated platform, integration and messaging costs. Discounts and refunded sales already removed from net sales are not deducted twice. Gross margin is a separate product-cost measure; contribution margin percentage is contribution divided by net sales, with no percentage when net sales is zero.</p>
      <p>Illustrative arithmetic only: 100 eligible customers per arm produce treatment net sales of $20,000 across 10 paid orders, versus $18,000 across 9 holdout orders. AOV is $2,000 in each arm. If total included costs are $14,000 and $12,500 respectively, contribution is $6,000 versus $5,500, or $60 versus $55 per eligible customer. The estimated difference is $5 per eligible customer, not $2,000 of proven SMS lift. Sampling uncertainty and any cross-arm differences still need assessment.</p>
      <p>Choose an observation period covering the actual consideration, payment and return cycle. Report quote acceptance, appointments, finance applications, deposits and settled orders separately; platform attribution is diagnostic rather than a causal result. Review contribution, opt-outs per delivered promotional recipient, complaint counts and adviser workload together. No automatic discount or expansion follows from a higher attributed revenue figure.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify card mt-8">
      <h2>Support, recovery and a controlled release</h2>
      <p>Name an owner for failed handoffs, stale data, duplicate sends, STOP/HELP routing and payment discrepancies. Define thresholds for pausing the affected workflow before the pilot. Preserve event logs, source versions and send decisions so support can explain what happened without asking the buyer to repeat sensitive details over SMS.</p>
      <p>Release a small eligible cohort after the proposed fixtures pass. If permission or state reconciliation fails, stop queued and scheduled sends, revoke obsolete quote links where supported and route unresolved cases to a representative. Before recovery, reconcile purchases, withdrawals, support holds and reservation expiries; discard stale backlog. Require an owner’s review of renewed eligibility before resuming. Rollback must preserve suppressions and retirement history in both systems and leave only one sender active.</p>
      <p>Continue with <a class="link" href="/guides/campaign-restraint">campaign restraint</a>, <a class="link" href="/guides/offer-discipline">offer discipline</a> and <a class="link" href="/guides/pricing">cost planning</a>. The <a class="link" href="/apps">app directory</a> can help form a shortlist; validate its claims against current supplier evidence and your own account tests.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FaqSection faqs={faqs} />
</BaseLayout>
